# Pantry — notes for the assistant

<!--
  Sample LOACHFILE.md. Copy it to the root of a workspace folder, name it
  LOACHFILE.md, and rewrite it for your project — Pantry is made up.

  - Plain Markdown, no special syntax. Loach adds the whole file to the
    system prompt on every turn, this comment included, so delete this
    block once you've adapted it.
  - It's read fresh each turn: an edit applies on your next send.
  - The first line shows in the tooltip of the LOACHFILE.md badge on the
    "Working in" notice, so make it say what the file is.
  - Anything past 32 KB is cut, but aim for a page: local models follow
    short instruction files far more reliably than long ones.
  - The model can list, find, read, search, write, edit, move and delete
    files in the folder, but it has no shell. Ask it to tell you which
